        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Second option: \\$2.72/L, compared with \\$2.80/L.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Second quantity}&=6\\times375\\text{ mL}\\\\\\text{Second quantity}&=2250\\text{ mL}=2.25\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{First unit price}&=\\frac{\\$5.60}{2\\text{ L}}=\\$2.80/\\text{L}\\\\\\text{Second unit price}&=\\frac{\\$6.12}{2.25\\text{ L}}=\\$2.72/\\text{L}\\end{align*}$$\nThe second option is the best buy because its price per litre is lower.",
